The approach is a 2^26-bit bitmap (8 MiB), which fits inside the 10 MiB limit. For each value I read its word, add 1 to the count if its bit was clear, and set the bit. That needs no final scan of the bitmap, so tiny inputs stay cheap. A prefetch 32 elements ahead hides the random-access latency. The bitmap comes from anonymous `mmap` (zeroed lazily) with a `MADV_HUGEPAGE` hint to cut page-fault and TLB cost, falling back to `calloc` if `mmap` fails. I have not compiled or run this.

