The values are below 2^26, so a bitmap of 2^26 bits (8 MiB) fits within the 10 MiB limit. Each element does a branchless test-and-set: the loop adds 1 to the count when the bit was previously clear, then sets it. This removes the final popcount pass over the bitmap.

